    "route": "nist_question",
    "answer": "Confabulation is a phenomenon in which GAI systems generate and confidently present erroneous or false content in response to prompts.  It also includes outputs that diverge from the prompts or other input or that contradict previously generated statements in the same context, and is colloquially referred to as “hallucinations” or “fabrications” [C1].  GAI outputs may further contain confabulated logic or citations that purport to justify the answer, potentially misleading humans into inappropriately trusting the system’s output [C3].",
